how did a canine companion keep stevo  sober where did the part-time stuntman  and full-time troublemaker get his  unmistakable voice and did he really go  to clown college this is the untold  truth of stevo  for stevo the path to jackass stardom  began long before the show itself he  told forbes that he first began  experimenting with videotaping when his  dad won a camera from a golf tournament  while the comedian was still a teenager  stevo took the camera from his dad's  closet and used it to film skateboard  tricks with his friends discovering that  he had a real knack and passion for  filming in the process it wasn't until  after stevo went to college at the  university of miami that he got the idea  to film more elaborate stunts he told  forbes i spent more time partying and  jumping off the diving boards at the  pool than going to class which was why i  got dumped by my girlfriend in the midst  of park break stevo turned back to  filming and started to videotape himself  performing dangerous stunts the  reactions he got from people who watched  his tapes convinced him to drop out of  school and become a performer  stevo's stint at the university of miami  wasn't the end of his education he later  attended the ringling brothers and  barnum and bailey clown college with 32  other classmates stevo told graham  bensinger that he got the opportunity to  work alongside another group of clowns  on a cruise ship the job only lasted a  season though because quote there was a  clown mutiny the other clowns didn't get  along with stevo and they all threatened  to leave if he returned for another  season so the management fired him  luckily the jump also gave stevo the  inspiration for a major stunt standing  on stilts stevo would light his clown  suit on fire then have a unicycler ride  through his legs while a skateboarder  jumped over his head and threw a  fireball that he spit out of his mouth  for the finale he'd chug a beer and tip  over stevo called jeff tremaine to pitch  the idea and they filmed the stunt as a  pilot for mtv the station refused to air  the stunt but liked the idea and stevo  enough to create jackass  who knew that being an over-the-top  stuntman could land you in jail stevo  found out the hard way in july 2002 when  a performance at a nightclub in  louisiana nearly landed him behind bars  with a felony two of the stunts in  stevo's performance came back to bite  him first he received a principle to  second-degree battery charge for  presiding over a stunt that ended in a  club bouncer knocking a college student  unconscious then he got a felony  obscenity charge for stapling his  scrotum to his thigh after much  negotiation first assistant district  attorney mark rhodes said that the  prosecution agreed that stevo hadn't  been an active participant in the  battery and that his scrotum stapling  was quote more than likely protected  under free speech when conducted in  front of paying adult patrons stevo  avoided charges and a trial by agreeing  to be on a probation for one year donate  five thousand dollars to a local shelter  for battered women and children and to  never perform in terrebonne again  the louisiana incident wasn't the last  time one of stevo's stunts led him into  legal troubles in fact he was arrested  again in sweden just a few months later  this time he swallowed a condom full of  marijuana and snuck it through customs  as a stunt for the don't try this at  home show he and his fellow jackass  members were performing in stockholm  stevo's fans know him as a stuntman and  some even know him as a stand-up  comedian but not many people are aware  of stevo the rapper back in 2011 he  recorded and released the album the  dumbest  hip-hop to not much fanfare at all the  cd included a bonus dvd of more stevo  content and a poster of the album cover  that read never before has a rapper been  so  dumb with tracks like crack cocaine and  popping off it's no surprise that  stevo's album didn't break the charts  but that was likely never his goal to  begin with even stevo's fans more or  less forgot the album entirely the  moment it was released stevo never  released a follow-up album and it  doesn't seem likely that he ever will  but fans can always go back and enjoy  one of the stranger moments in the  stuntman's career for themselves  stevo went through a massive lifestyle  change in the late 2000s after years of  performing wild stunts partially fueled  by drugs and alcohol he decided to get  sober and he's maintained that sobriety  since 2008. when talking about it stevo  makes what was likely a lengthy and  difficult decision seemed totally simple  he told men's health here's what got me  motivated to change i hit a wall i  really reached a point where thank god  my life got so bad that i had to  surrender to the process of recovery the  process has entirely transformed his  life and it's left him with plenty of  energy for more stunts of course no one  goes through recovery alone and stevo  credits his rescue dogs walter and  bernie with keeping him going he adopted  his first dog when he first embarked on  the recovery journey in 2008 and he said  it's been good for him to quote have a  priority that's not myself since then  stevo's dogs have become his closest  friends they've helped to deepen his  connection with animals in general and  that's become a major part of his life  stevo has been an outspoken animal  rights activist for years and sometimes  he combines his passion for ridiculous  stunts with his love of animals to  powerful results in 2014 stevo and five  of his friends changed a sea world drive  sign just outside of san diego to say  sea world sucks doing that was wrong i  don't want to be right  that got people talking not as much as  stevo might have wanted so the following  year he upped the ante stevo knows how  to get attention and climbing a 100 foot  crane certainly did the trick the  machine hovered above sunset boulevard  which gave the performer the perfect  spot to speak to the world through a  giant shamu balloon with just two words  on it sea world sucks at the top of the  crane stevo set off a series of  fireworks before making his way back to  the ground where he was promptly  arrested from the streets below law  enforcement couldn't tell whether the  man on the crane was suicidal so they  deployed a whole team to air on the side  of caution a helicopter five ambulances  and close to 100 firefighters  prosecutors charged stevo with five  misdemeanors that could have landed him  in jail for more than four years he  reached a plea deal for 30 days in jail  three years probation and a 14 000  reimbursement to the city of los angeles  in the end stevo reported for his  sentence at twin towers correctional  facility but he was released after  serving less than eight hours  in addition to fighting for animal  rights with attention-grabbing public  displays stevo also altered his own  lifestyle to align with his values he  told us weekly that he became a vegan  shortly after he started his recovery  and the decision impacted way more than  his diet he said i think it's benefited  every area of my life  since that interview stevo hasn't gone  back to his meat-eating ways but these  days he says that he's not vegan he's  technically a pescetarian because he'll  eat fish and eggs from time to time  that's not his biggest slip-up though he  told men's health i've been letting a  lot of dairy slide too even admitting  that i have a problem with that despite  having been a vegan himself stevo has  also been critical of vegans in the past  he wrote on instagram to all the  combative annoying vegans who are  choosing to attack me for not forcing  veganism on my cats and for not being a  strict militant vegan myself maybe stop  working so hard to pit people who are on  your team against you the post garnered  plenty of backlash from some vegan  commenters but stevo has never been one  to care about haters  every jackass fan is familiar with  stevo's voice there's just nothing quite  like it he has the gravelly rumble of a  cigarette smoking blues singer but he  sounded like that for over 20 years i  always thought that my world record for  barfing the most on television might  have something to do with it over the  years he's also speculated that his  unique tone could have come from  swallowing glass or consuming copious  amounts of nitrous oxide in his younger  years eventually stevo decided to  consult with the doctor to find out the  root of his raspy voice and the answer  wasn't at all what he expected it turns  out stevo sounds that way because he  uses his throat muscles rather than his  vocal cords to talk to prevent his  condition from getting worse stevo  started working on using his vocal cords  with a voice coach but he wasn't  entirely sold on changing his signature  sound but i don't even know if i want my  voice to change i kind of like getting  recognized over the phone and my girl  darn sure doesn't want it any different  no i love your voice  chances are even if stevo learns how to  talk the right way he'll continue to  sound like he always has  after making his name as a stuntman  stevo decided to stretch his abilities  and try out a new career path he began  working as a stand-up comedian in 2011  and he spent the past decade touring  various shows and approaching stand-up  with the same determination he once  aimed at his stuntman ambitions stevo  has completed two comedy specials gnarly  which was the first special he took on  tour and the bucket list which she began  touring just as the coronavirus pandemic  shuttered venues across the country his  stand-up acts have always incorporated  some of his stuntman roots but the  bucket list takes things to a whole new  level notably he incorporates footage of  brand new stunts and stories into his  act creating a multimedia experience for  the audience despite all the work that  stevo has put into a stand-up axe he's  had a difficult time getting them out to  anyone who isn't in his live audience he  would gladly give the axe to a streaming  platform like netflix but so far there  hasn't been any interest in his work he  spoke to graham bensinger in 2019  regarding the possibility of his getting  a comedy special on netflix that they  only want to give them to the most  prestigious  pure  you know lifelong stand-up comedians  of which they do not consider me to be  one in the same interview with graham  bensinger stevo explained that he and  his fiancee lux wright met on a job that  never ended up seeing the light of day  even though the project ended up being a  failure it gave stevo the opportunity to  meet the love of his life the two of  them don't plan on ever having kids but  they still have big plans for their  future opening an animal sanctuary where  they'll eventually be able to live when  they retire you don't have to know us  very well to know that we love animals  stevo told bensinger we want to have it  in southern california so we can drive  to it  ideally it would also operate as a bed  and breakfast that would give people the  opportunity to stay longer and develop  deeper relationships with the animals  they're visiting stevo said he hopes it  gives people pause the next time they go  to eat an animal for dinner he went on  to explain in the long term the  sanctuary would also become a daycare  for children with special needs stevo's  nephew has down syndrome and autism and  he has witnessed the stress his sister  has put under while trying to manage her  career and take care of her children he  wants to be able to give back to parents  with similar struggles and his fiancee  is more than happy to create that legacy  with him check out one of our newest  videos right here plus even more looper  videos about your favorite celebrities  are coming soon subscribe to our youtube  channel and hit the bell so you don't  miss a single one  [Music]

